<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dublin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dublin is the capital and largest city of Ireland, at the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-liffey">River Liffey</a> on the east coast. Founded as a Norse settlement in the 9th century, it became the centre of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> kingdom and, after the Anglo-Norman invasion of 1169–1171, the seat of English government in Ireland. It was the scene of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-rising">Easter Rising</a> of 1916 and became the capital of the independent Irish state in 1922.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dublin.jpg" alt="Dublin" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 瑞丽江的河水 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dublin_-_aerial_-_2025-07-07_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
